WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.503
-Our first guest tonight is a
very funny comedian and actor

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:04.904
you know from
"The King of Staten Island"

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:06.439
and "Saturday Night Live."
He stars in the new

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:07.873
animated series
"The Freak Brothers,"

00:00:07.873 --> 00:00:10.309
which is streaming exclusively
on Tubi November 14th.

00:00:10.309 --> 00:00:11.744
Please welcome back to the show

00:00:11.744 --> 00:00:14.514
our friend Pete Davidson,
everybody.

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:16.549
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:22.388 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:28.227 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:28.227 --> 00:00:29.595
Welcome back.
-Hello.

00:00:29.595 --> 00:00:32.031
-It's nice to see you.
-Good to see you, too.

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:33.466
-This --
I was going to say thanks --

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:35.468
You know, you were just down
the hall, but you actually --

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:36.969
This is very on-brand
for Pete Davidson.

00:00:36.969 --> 00:00:38.904
We were worried you weren't
gonna make it here on time

00:00:38.904 --> 00:00:40.940
'cause you were stuck in traffic
on the Verrazzano Bridge.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:45.077
-Yes. 30 minutes ago,
I was on the Verrazzano Bridge.

00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:46.746
-This is very impressive
that you made it.

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:48.414
And I can't thank you enough.

00:00:48.414 --> 00:00:49.748
-Oh, that's -- You know,
I'm excited to be here.

00:00:49.748 --> 00:00:52.251
Thanks for having me.
-I want to address something.

00:00:52.251 --> 00:00:55.121
I feel like I want to confirm
if it's real...

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:57.056
-Okay.
-...or a rumor.

00:00:57.056 --> 00:00:59.291
You've been reading a lot
about it in the press.

00:00:59.291 --> 00:01:01.494
-Yeah, you know,
I've been wanting to talk

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:03.530
about this because --
-Thank you.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.464
We appreciate you doing it here.

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:07.066
-There's a lot of people
I walk by.

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:08.267
People are, like, whispering,

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:11.571
and, you know,
making eyes at me.

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:14.207
And, you know, but it is true --

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:16.642
I do have a show on Tubi
coming out.

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:18.044
-Tubi.
-Yeah.

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:20.479
-The Tubi.
-The Tubi.

00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:24.850
A lot of people are shocked
I could get on a show like Tubi.

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:28.187
-Yeah. But it's a real --

00:01:28.187 --> 00:01:31.357
-It's a real thing. Tubi. Yeah.

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:34.527
-Yeah. That's exciting.
-Yes. Thank you.

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:37.196
-And, you know, you are --
'cause you do a lot of stand-up.

00:01:37.196 --> 00:01:39.198
Obviously, we know
from you "SNL," as well.

00:01:39.198 --> 00:01:40.967
-Yeah.
-First time doing animated.

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:43.870
-Yes.
-It seems like a scam.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.272
-It's a dream.
You just get to sit --

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:48.841
You go --
I got to do it in my closet.

00:01:48.841 --> 00:01:50.243
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:52.645
-Now, was it the closet
because of the pandemic or...?

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:56.249
-No, I just requested it.
That was -- Yeah.

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:58.183
No, it was during the pandemic,
and they called.

00:01:58.183 --> 00:02:00.720
And they were like,
"Would you like to do a cartoon

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.055
with Woody Harrelson,
John Goodman,

00:02:03.055 --> 00:02:05.258
Tiffany Haddish, La La Anthony,

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.560
Adam DeVine,
and Blake Anderson?"

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.228
I was like, "Yeah."

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:11.297
I was like, "What's the --
What's the premise?""

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:14.033
They're like, "You're a pothead
that smokes weed all the time."

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:18.871
I was like, "Yeah. For sure.
Absolutely. Yeah."

00:02:18.871 --> 00:02:20.840
-As an actor,
you've always said to me

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.308
you want to stretch.

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:25.077
-Yeah, I need to stretch
my legs a little bit.

00:02:25.077 --> 00:02:26.479
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:29.048
-You want to challenge yourself
to do different things.

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:30.949
-Yeah, absolutely.

00:02:30.949 --> 00:02:32.251
-That is really
an all-star cast.

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:33.486
-Yeah.
-You have to tell us --

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:35.254
I think you are --

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:37.289
you are the middle
of these three gentlemen, right?

00:02:37.289 --> 00:02:39.192
-Yes, that is me.

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:40.593
-Yeah.

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:43.663
-That is Phineas Freakers.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:45.264
-Yeah.
-He is, you know,

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:47.000
the kind of nerdy --

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:50.302
He thinks he's really smart,
leader of the Freak Brothers.

00:02:50.302 --> 00:02:53.606
-Yeah.
-And that is me.

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:56.075
-Now, this kind of has the style

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:59.045
that plays into this premise,
because this --

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:01.747
You guys are '60s stoners...
-Right.

00:03:01.747 --> 00:03:03.516
-...who come
to the modern times.

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:05.784
It's a very high-concept
stoner cartoon.

00:03:05.784 --> 00:03:08.020
-You know, everybody is into,
like, "Tenet" and [bleep].

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:09.856
But this is --

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:12.758
-Can we talk about that?
Everybody's into "Tenet."

00:03:12.758 --> 00:03:14.227
-"Tenet" and [bleep].
But listen.

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:18.665
This -- This story
really spoke to me.

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:21.768
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.768 --> 00:03:23.002
-'Cause that's the thing.
The two things --

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.370
When you answer the phone,

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.238
you want to be challenged
in the part...

00:03:26.238 --> 00:03:27.340
-Yes, challenged.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:28.607
-...and the script
has to speak to you.

00:03:28.607 --> 00:03:29.842
-Absolutely.
-Yeah.

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:33.879
-And they were like --
The story is...

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:38.918
that these three gentlemen
smoke a mega doobie

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:41.720
in 1969.

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:45.023
And they wake up in 2021.

00:03:45.023 --> 00:03:46.459
-There you go. And --

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:48.861
-So you know what?
So enough about "Tenet."

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:50.329
-Yeah.
-We get it.

00:03:50.329 --> 00:03:53.165
-You can only imagine
what these fellas get into.

00:03:53.165 --> 00:03:56.702 line:0%
-And this is -- this is --
-That's Tiffany Haddish.

00:03:56.702 --> 00:03:58.070 line:0%
-That's Tiffany Haddish.
-Yeah.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:03:59.438 line:0%
-For real?
-Yeah, no, for real.

00:03:59.438 --> 00:04:01.374
-She is a talking cat.
-She is a talking cat.

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:04.210
-Who's sort of your guide.
-Yes.

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:06.745
-Yeah.
-Yeah, she's the best.

00:04:06.745 --> 00:04:10.249
-Do you find when you're
in the closet recording...

00:04:10.249 --> 00:04:12.184
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.184 --> 00:04:14.887
Do you find, like --
They're listening in real time

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:16.789
or do you record it
and send it off?

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:19.525
-They're there with you,
which is very --

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:20.693
-Not in the closet with you.

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:22.729
-No, they're not
in the closet with me.

00:04:22.729 --> 00:04:24.497
But my --

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:27.066
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:30.503
They watch you do it,
which is always weird,

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:33.473
because you'll do, like --
You're screaming in your closet.

00:04:33.473 --> 00:04:35.007
-Yeah.

00:04:35.007 --> 00:04:37.343
-And then they'll be like,
"Yeah, that was really good.

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:41.080
Let's do it again
and in a completely different

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.916
other way
that wasn't like what you did."

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:45.384
But we had fun doing it.

00:04:45.384 --> 00:04:48.020
It was just something really
nice to do during the pandemic.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.756
-I am a huge fan of your mom...
-Yes.

00:04:50.756 --> 00:04:53.125
-...who is one of the
sweetest ladies in the world.

00:04:53.125 --> 00:04:56.828
-Me, as well.
Amy Davidson. Good lady.

00:04:56.828 --> 00:04:58.864
-Now, is Amy --
During this time,

00:04:58.864 --> 00:05:01.100
were you and Amy
under the same roof?

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.436
Was she there when you would,
like, skulk off to the closet?

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:04.637
And did she believe you

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:06.038
when you told her
you were doing a cartoon?

00:05:06.038 --> 00:05:09.274
-Yeah. I'm just like --

00:05:09.274 --> 00:05:12.144
We did live together
for like a good two years,

00:05:12.144 --> 00:05:14.146
and she was
a pretty great roommate.

00:05:14.146 --> 00:05:17.716
-Yeah. How would you --
What do you think

00:05:17.716 --> 00:05:19.518
she would say
about you as a roommate?

00:05:19.518 --> 00:05:23.255
-I think she would just be like,
"That kid jerks off a lot."

00:05:23.255 --> 00:05:24.957
Like...like...

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:26.992
[ Laughter ]

00:05:26.992 --> 00:05:29.595
-I will say, I do believe this.

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:32.464
If a mom said it, I do think
they wouldn't say your name.

00:05:32.464 --> 00:05:33.799
They'd say "that kid."
-"That kid."

00:05:33.799 --> 00:05:35.735
-They'd be like,
"Pete's on 'SNL.'

00:05:35.735 --> 00:05:38.304
Pete's in the movies.
Pete's got a show on Tubi.

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:39.938
That kid jerks off a lot."
-"That kid jerks off a lot."

00:05:39.938 --> 00:05:43.375
Yeah. No. But we had
a really good situation.

00:05:43.375 --> 00:05:44.710
It was really -- It was like --

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:47.145
We got really close
and really tight. I enjoyed it.

00:05:47.145 --> 00:05:48.447
-That's really awesome.
-Yeah.

00:05:48.447 --> 00:05:49.615
-Does she -- What --

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:52.518
Of your stuff,
what does she like the most?

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:54.720
I mean, she must have liked
the fact

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:56.989
that you did a film
in Staten Island.

00:05:56.989 --> 00:05:58.558
-Yeah, I think she's just happy

00:05:58.558 --> 00:06:00.759
I'm not, like, selling crack
under the bridge.

00:06:00.759 --> 00:06:04.463
You know, because, like,
that's definitely my calling.

00:06:04.463 --> 00:06:09.802
So, yeah, she's just --
she's pleased with anything.

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:11.270
But every once in a while,
she is --

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:13.238
You can tell
she's still a little unsure

00:06:13.238 --> 00:06:17.477
